1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,059
Welcome to Stock Portfolio Analyzer.

2
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:11,530
Turn your transaction history into a clear picture of what you own, how your investments are allocated, and how your portfolio has performed.

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,052
Start in Input Transactions.

4
00:00:14,052 --> 00:00:20,605
Upload a CSV with the ticker, date, buy or sell type, quantity, and price.

5
00:00:20,605 --> 00:00:26,690
Here, we load the included sample data: trades in Apple, Microsoft, and Tesla.

6
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:30,092
You can also enter an individual trade.

7
00:00:30,092 --> 00:00:35,989
Choose the date and transaction type, then enter the symbol, quantity, and price per share.

8
00:00:35,989 --> 00:00:39,920
Review the details, then use Add transaction to save it.

9
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,483
Next, open Current Portfolio.

10
00:00:42,483 --> 00:00:52,046
The summary shows the value of your remaining shares, their cost basis, unrealized gains, and profit already realized through sales.

11
00:00:52,046 --> 00:00:56,350
The allocation chart shows how much each stock contributes.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,261
The stock breakdown lets you compare quantities, average cost, prices, gains, and allocation.

13
00:01:03,261 --> 00:01:08,559
This demo uses last transaction prices, with live pricing switched off.

14
00:01:08,559 --> 00:01:11,930
The Price Source column makes that clear.

15
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:18,716
Historical Performance brings the full journey together: total investment, sales, remaining value, and total return.

16
00:01:18,716 --> 00:01:26,080
X I R R is the annualized return that accounts for the timing of each buy and sell.

17
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:31,509
Finally, compare portfolio value with net money invested over time.

18
00:01:31,509 --> 00:01:35,809
With live pricing off, this chart uses transaction prices.

19
00:01:35,809 --> 00:01:40,110
Enable Yahoo Finance pricing for market data when available.

20
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:48,200
That is Stock Portfolio Analyzer: import your trades, understand your holdings, and track performance in one place.

21
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:53,890
Try the sample portfolio to explore the app before adding your own transactions.
